What is the different between while and do while ?
    In while, condition will be checking first, after that the body will be exected.
   Where as in the case of do while do body will be executed atleast once for the first time without checking any condition.

  Syntax:
do
{
  do body;
}
while(condition);

eg:
// Online C compiler to run C program online
#include <stdio.h>

int main() {
   int a=1;
   do{
       printf("happy people ");
       a++;
   }
  while(a>=5);   //false
    
    return 0;
}
output:
happy people 

